{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And behold the plague is in the walls of the house.</b> Up to here ten plagues have been mentioned: six upon a person's body, and they are שאת, ספחת, בהרת, שחין, נתק, and מריטת הראש. Four outside the body: in a woolen garment, in a linen garment, in every leather utensil, and in the walls of the house." "<b>And you will find</b> the pericopes arranged in this order, and the plagues are ten, corresponding to the Ten Commandments. When Israel would fulfill the Torah and the commandments in the land, they would be saved from them; and if not, they would be afflicted by them." "<b>Depressed hollows.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that their appearance was sunken. And the reason the passage comes in plural language — וחלצו את האבנים והשליכו ושרפו ולקחו והביאו — is that he and his neighbor are both liable for the removal and partners in the building, for concerning this they said: woe to the wicked and woe to his neighbor. But afterward it returns to speak in singular language — יקציע את הבית, and likewise יקח וטח — to make clear that he alone, upon whose wall the plague is, is liable for the expenses of the קציעה, which is the scraping, and the taking of the dust for plaster and plastering."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:25.030191405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}